messages.content:
Analyze the Jira bug report title and description and the seed changes that were made to fix the reported bug. Combine this analysis with the initial static impact set, which contains the fully qualified names of code entities that are statically related to the seed changes.
For each entity in the initial static impact set, analyze its relationship to the seed changes and collect evidence indicating whether the entity must be modified as a consequence of the seed changes.  Furthermore, identify any additional code entities that must be modified or created and collect supporting evidence.
Focus on production code, not test code or other files.
Inputs: - Jira bug report title: When in ssh plugin we does not set username in scheme, Ivy always try to connect with guest username, even if we change one in panel. - Jira bug report description: When in ssh plugin we does not set username in scheme, Ivy always try to connect with username 'guest', even if we change one in panel.
(It is becouse CredentialPanel is shown from SshCache.getSession(), where user is already set.) - Seed changes and their Git diff hunks: [{"fqn": "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.getSession(java.lang.String)", "git_diff_hunk": "@@ -81,0 +94,9 @@ public abstract class AbstractSshBasedRepository extends AbstractRepository {
+ if (user == null) {
+ Credentials c = requestCredentials(host);
+ if (c != null) {
+ user = c.getUserName();
+ userPassword = c.getPasswd();
+ } else {
+ Message.error("username is not set");
+ }
+ }"}] - Initial static code change impact set: ["org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.sftp.SFTPRepository.getSftpChannel(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.getHost()", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.getKeyFile()", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.getKeyFilePassword()", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.getPassFile()", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.getPort()", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.getRepositoryScheme()", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.getUser()", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.getUserPassword()", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.host", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.keyFile", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.keyFilePassword", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.parseURI(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.passFile", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.port", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.setHost(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.setKeyFile(java.io.File)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.setKeyFilePassword(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.setPassFile(java.io.File)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.setPort(int)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.setUser(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.setUserPassword(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.user", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.AbstractSshBasedRepository.userPassword", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.SshCache.CfUserInfo.CfUserInfo(java.lang.String,java.lang.String,java.lang.String,java.io.File,java.lang.String,java.io.File)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.SshCache.Entry.getSession()", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.SshCache.getCacheEntry(java.lang.String,java.lang.String,int)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.SshCache.getInstance()", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.SshCache.getSession(java.lang.String,int,java.lang.String,java.lang.String,java.io.File,java.lang.String,java.io.File)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.SshCache.requestCredentials(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.SshCache.setSession(java.lang.String,java.lang.String,int,com.jcraft.jsch.Session)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.SshRepository.get(java.lang.String,java.io.File)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.SshRepository.list(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.SshRepository.openStream(org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.SshResource)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.SshRepository.put(java.io.File,java.lang.String,boolean)", "org.apache.ivy.plugins.repository.ssh.SshRepository.resolveResource(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.ivy.util.Message.error(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.ivy.util.Message.requestCredentials(java.lang.String)", "org.apache.ivy.util.Message.verbose(java.lang.String)"]

Expected output:
Structured evidence for each entity of the initial static impact set, including: - its fully qualified name - an assessment of whether it must be modified as a consequence of the seed changes - the supporting evidence
Additionally, include any code entities that must be modified or created but are not part of the initial static impact set.
